    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7yNO4e",
      "title": "feat: re-add OPCM V800 templates with simplified super-permissioned args",
      "author": "OptimismBot",
      "number": 1502,
      "body": "> **Draft — do not merge until the V800 OPCM is deployed on-chain.**\n\nRe-adds the `OPCMUpgradeV800` and `OPCMMigrateV800` templates, their integration tests, and example tasks that were removed in #1501, now carrying the simplified super-permissioned game arg layout from #1500.\n\nStacked on #1501 (base branch `centaur/remove-opcm-v800-templates`). GitHub will retarget this to `main` once #1501 merges.\n\n## What changed vs the original V800 templates\n`OPCMUpgradeV800` encodes `SUPER_PERMISSIONED_CANNON` (gt=5) game args as **proposer-only** (`abi.encode(a.proposer)`, 32 bytes) instead of the old `abi.encode(absolutePrestate, proposer, challenger)`, matching the simplified op-contracts V800 ABI. Test coverage in `SuperRootUpgrade.t.sol` is updated accordingly, and `test_upgrade_sepolia()` is dropped because the forked OPCM predates the new layout. This is the exact diff from #1500.\n\n## Why draft\nV800 is not yet deployed on-chain, so `template_regression_tests` cannot simulate `035-opcm-upgrade-v800` against a compatible OPCM — it reverts in `_build`. By removing the templates from `main` (#1501) and re-adding the new version here, we avoid carrying a backwards-compatibility shim for a not-yet-live OPCM. Once V800 is deployed: merge #1501, then mark this ready and merge.\n\nCloses #1466 (once merged)\n\nPrompted by: @mds1\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-15T20:34:18Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 1662,
      "deletions": 0
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7x2C5P",
      "title": "fix: simplify OPCM V800 super permissioned game args",
      "author": "ajsutton",
      "number": 1500,
      "body": "Updates `OPCMUpgradeV800` to encode `SUPER_PERMISSIONED_CANNON` game args as proposer-only, matching the simplified op-contracts ABI. Updates fork-backed config coverage and removes execution against the pre-change Sepolia OPCM fixture.\n\nCloses ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops#1466\n\nTest plan:\n- `forge build --deny-warnings`\n- `forge test --match-contract 'SuperRootUpgrade(Test|SetupValidationTest)' -vvv`\n- `forge fmt --check src/template/OPCMUpgradeV800.sol test/integration/SuperRootUpgrade.t.sol`\n- `./src/script/check-struct-order.sh`\n\nFull `forge test`: 299 passed; 2 unrelated integration tests require unavailable external/local RPC services.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
      "createdAt": "2026-07-15T03:21:35Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 10,
      "deletions": 86
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOKIsnqM7yNNdv",
      "title": "chore: remove OPCM V800 templates (merged too early)",
      "author": "OptimismBot",
      "number": 1501,
      "body": "Removes the `OPCMUpgradeV800` and `OPCMMigrateV800` templates, their integration tests, and example tasks.\n\n## Why\nThese V800 templates were landed before the V800 OPCM is deployed on-chain. The `template_regression_tests` job simulates the example task `035-opcm-upgrade-v800` end-to-end against the current/forked OPCM, which predates the new arg layout and reverts (`OPCMUpgradeV800: Delegatecall failed in _build.`). This is the same wall that #1500 hit.\n\nRather than carry backwards-compatible encoding for an OPCM that isn't live yet, we remove the templates now. They are re-added — with the simplified proposer-only `SUPER_PERMISSIONED_CANNON` game arg layout from #1500 — in a follow-up **draft** PR that stays ready to merge once V800 is deployed.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/template/OPCMUpgradeV800.sol`, `src/template/OPCMMigrateV800.sol` (Migrate imports interfaces from Upgrade, so both move together)\n- `test/integration/SuperRootUpgrade.t.sol`, `test/integration/SuperRootMigrate.t.sol`\n- `test/tasks/example/sep/035-opcm-upgrade-v800/`, `test/tasks/example/sep/036-opcm-migrate-v800/`\n- `src/ci.just`: drop the now-unneeded `036-opcm-migrate-v800` skip block\n\n## Follow-up\nRe-add draft PR: (linked once opened)\n\nPrompted by: @mds1\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-ops",
